{"affected":[{"defaultStatus":"unknown","original_ranges":[{"status":"affected","version":"8.4.65"}],"product":"Ultralytics","vendor":"Ultralytics"}],"aliases":["CVE-2026-118618"],"assertions":[{"affected_indices":[0],"datePublic":"2026-10-28T16:31:30.095Z","descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Ultralytics parse_model Code Injection Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Ultralytics. User interaction is required to exploit this vulnerability in that the target must visit a malicious page or open a malicious file.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the parse_model function. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of a user-supplied string before using it to execute Python code. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of the current user. Was ZDI-CAN-30121."}],"metrics":[{"cvssV3_0":{"baseScore":7.8,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","vectorString":"CVSS:3.0/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","version":"3.0"},"format":"CVSS"}],"problemTypes":[{"descriptions":[{"cweId":"CWE-94","description":"CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')","lang":"en","type":"CWE"}]}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-10-28T16:54:29.943Z","orgId":"99f1926a-a320-47d8-bbb5-42feb611262e","shortName":"zdi"},"role":"cna","title":"Ultralytics parse_model Code Injection Remote Code Execution Vulnerability"},{"affected_indices":[],"metrics":[{"other":{"content":{"id":"CVE-2026-118618","options":[{"Exploitation":"none"},{"Automatable":"no"},{"Technical Impact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:07:03.114728Z","version":"2.0.3"},"type":"ssvc"}}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-11-05T17:07:19.437Z","orgId":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","shortName":"CISA-ADP"},"role":"adp","title":"CISA ADP Vulnrichment"}],"assessment":{"authentication":null,"classifier_version":"1.0","confidence":"unknown","configuration":null,"e